# SVE Data Vault — environment variables
#
# Names and safe placeholders only, verified against the code that reads
# them. Copy to a real .env for local `npm run dev` / `npm run migrate`
# use; never commit the real file.

# --- Database (required) ---
# Same physical database as platform-services/identity — Data Vault's
# tables (002_data-vault-foundation) live alongside Identity's own
# schema; there is one shared Postgres database, not two.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://sve_identity:replace-with-a-real-password@localhost:5432/sve_identity_dev

# --- SVEGIP session bridge (optional) ---
# Read via platform-services/identity's SecretsProvider/svegipSessionBridge
# (src/composition/container.ts imports identity's loadSvegipBridgeSecret) —
# must be the EXACT SAME value already configured for apps/svegip's own
# Netlify environment (SVEGIP_SESSION_SECRET in
# apps/svegip/netlify/functions/_auth-core.mts). Not a new secret. If
# unset, requests using only a SVEGIP cookie are simply not authenticated.
SVEGIP_SESSION_SECRET=replace-with-the-same-value-configured-in-svegip

# --- CSRF/origin protection for SVEGIP-cookie-authenticated writes (required to accept cookie-authenticated POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE) ---
# Comma-separated list of exact origins (scheme://host[:port]) trusted to
# make state-changing Data Vault requests using the SVEGIP cookie bridge.
# This is NOT a secret — it is public configuration, deliberately kept out
# of application/domain logic so it can differ per environment without a
# code change (see src/config/trustedOrigins.ts). Native bearer-token
# requests are never subject to this check (see docs/architecture/
# data-vault-foundation.md "CSRF/origin protection"). Behind the eventual
# same-origin Netlify reverse proxy, this should be set to the exact
# origin apps/svegip is served from (e.g. https://portal.example.sve) —
# never left unset in any environment that enables the SVEGIP bridge.
SVE_DATA_VAULT_TRUSTED_ORIGINS=https://replace-with-svegip-origin.example

# --- Local dev server (optional) ---
PORT=4002
